#!/bin/bash
# land-one-bag.sh — one bag, on the server, and a checkout worth the name.
#
# BOTH SIDES (together-city-chat + together-city-react). Vercel AND Railway.
# NO DATABASE MIGRATION — the bag lives in the profile's existing JSON column.
# PRECONDITION: land-first-stone-first.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="A bag that forgets"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"Which one do I buy first"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-first-stone-first.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="d22c56a65ea6ea29db95c4a95cf42962c3a3897ae40f5fa2c41057a31d7125d5"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

echo "== gates: the API"
cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/beauty src/astrology
cd ..

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/src/beauty \
        together-city-react/src/features/beauty \
        together-city-react/src/app/one-bag.test.ts
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
A bag that forgets is worse than no bag

THE HUB HAD TWO BAGS. The routine kept one in a React state and the market kept
another. A citizen could be looking at "3 items - 2,098" on one page and "10
items - 6,009" on the other at the same moment, each with its own total and its
own checkout button, and both were correct in the sense that neither was.
Following a link erased whichever one they were not looking at. A bag that
forgets is worse than no bag, because it invites the work of filling it twice.

ONE BAG NOW, ON THE SERVER, PER CITIZEN. It survives navigation because it is
not in the page; it survives a reload and a second device for the same reason.
It empties on exactly two events — the citizen empties it, or an order is placed
— and on nothing else.

NO MIGRATION. It lives in `extras.bag`, the profile's existing JSON column, and
that key was chosen with the last collision in mind: `budget` is the onboarding
STRING answer and `monthlyBudget` is the per-category object, and writing an
object over that string once took the market, the routine and the profile down
together with a single TypeError. So a key nothing else uses, and a shape check
on the way out rather than a cast. A stored blob is not a type, and one-bag.spec
feeds it a string, a number, an object, a nested array and a line whose id is a
number to prove it.

IDS AND QUANTITIES ONLY, NEVER PRICES. A bag holding its own prices is a bag
that can disagree with the shelf: add at 369, the price moves, and checkout
charges whichever number the browser kept. Every rupee is looked up at read
time, which is the rule payment has always followed. A product withdrawn from
the catalogue leaves the bag and the page says how many went, rather than
quietly shortening a total somebody had already read.

AND CHECKOUT IS A PAGE NOW, NOT A SHEET. It used to open the wallet over
whatever screen you were on, asking somebody to authorise a charge against a
list summarised as one grey line of comma-separated running text with no prices
in it — ten products wrapped over three lines. That is a confirmation dialog
with a total on it.

The bar is a link, and it goes to My Orders: every line with its photograph, its
own price, its quantity and its line total; the total at the foot; the city
wallet under that. The photograph travels with the line, joined on the server
for the same reason the price is — the shelf is the only thing that knows, and
the last screen before paying should not be the first one without pictures.
Quantities are editable there too, because the last place somebody reads a list
is exactly where they change their mind about it, and sending them back to the
shop to drop one item is how a bag gets abandoned instead of trimmed.

Once it is paid for the bag empties itself and becomes the first row underneath,
and the page goes back to being what it is called.
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: A bag that forgets is worse than no bag
 Both sides — push, then give Railway a minute. The bag is
 stored per citizen, so it will be empty once after deploy.
===============================================================

DONE
